.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt WAIT 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm waitpid ,
.Nm wait4
.Nd wait for a child to change state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/wait.h
.Ft pid_t
.Fn waitpid "pid_t pid" "int *status" "int options"
.Ft pid_t
.Fn wait4 "pid_t pid" "int *status" "int options" "struct rusage *rusage"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn waitpid
waits for a state change in a child selected by
.Fa pid :
.Bl -tag -width "Greater than 0"
.It Greater than 0
The child with that process ID.
.It -1
Any child.
.It 0
Any child in the caller's process group.
.It Less than -1
Any child whose process group ID equals
.Li -pid .
The value -2147483648 matches no child.
.El
.Pp
By default, the call waits for a child to exit and reaps it.
The
.Fa options
argument may combine these bits:
.Bl -tag -width "WCONTINUED (8)"
.It Dv WNOHANG No (1)
Return 0 if a matching child exists but has no reportable state change.
.It Dv WUNTRACED No (2)
Also report a stopped child.
.It Dv WCONTINUED No (8)
Also report a continued child.
.El
.Pp
Other option bits are ignored.
Stop and continue events are reported once and do not reap the child.
.Pp
If
.Fa status
is not null, it receives the Linux-encoded wait status.
Use
.Dv WIFEXITED
and
.Dv WEXITSTATUS
for normal exit,
.Dv WIFSIGNALED
and
.Dv WTERMSIG
for signal death,
.Dv WIFSTOPPED
and
.Dv WSTOPSIG
for a stop, and
.Dv WIFCONTINUED
for a continuation.
.Pp
.Fn wait4
performs the same wait and accepts an optional
.Fa rusage
pointer.
On reap, the kernel zeroes the 72-byte i386 resource usage structure;
per-process resource usage is not tracked.
Stop and continue reports do not fill this structure.
Nonnull status and resource usage pointers are checked for write
access before any child is reaped.
.Pp
The i386 system call numbers are 7 for
.Nm waitpid
and 114 for
.Nm wait4 .
EBX contains
.Fa pid ,
ECX the status pointer, and EDX the options.
For
.Nm wait4 ,
ESI contains the resource usage pointer.
Musl's
.Fn wait
and
.Fn waitpid
use the
.Nm wait4
system call.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return the process ID of the child whose state was
reported, or 0 when
.Dv WNOHANG
finds a matching child but no reportable event.
On failure they return -1 and set
.Va errno .
The kernel returns a negative error number on failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The default suite's
.Pa tests/forktest.c
forks a child that exits with status 42, waits for it, and checks
.Dv WIFEXITED
and
.Dv WEXITSTATUS .
.Pa tests/jobprobe.c
stops a child and waits with
.Dv WUNTRACED ,
continues it and waits with
.Dv WCONTINUED ,
then kills it and checks the reported signal.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[ECHILD]"
.It Bq Er ECHILD
No child matches
.Fa pid .
.It Bq Er EFAULT
A nonnull status or resource usage pointer does not refer to writable
user memory.
.It Bq Er EINTR
A deliverable signal is pending while the call would otherwise block.
.It Bq Er ESRCH
There is no current process.
.El
